{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"RCA (confirmed, rebar-debug protocol): epic 2f4c-7e5c-e782-4e97 closed with a PASS COMPLETION_VERDICT (verified_at_sha 52cd34f) but no signed completion attestation. Mechanism: commit 9ba1e90 (bug 330c, landed 2026-08-03T03:37Z) added checkbox-state normalization to material_fingerprint (pass1.py) with no grandfathering. compute_validity (attest.py, completion-verifier branch) recomputes with the NEW algorithm and compares to the manifest-frozen 'material:' hash. Children 433c/9d07/a584/d3ed were closed+signed 2026-08-02 (pre-330c) with fully-checked ACs (required by the 433c close gate), so their signed hashes embed [x]; the normalized recompute can never match -> stale-material -> child_closure_findings marks them uncertified -> gate_ops sets certifiable=False -> transition_close.py 'certifiable is False' early-return skips signing SILENTLY (no stderr, and the PASS sidecar drops certifiable/summary). Discriminating experiment: recomputing each invalid child's fingerprint over the LEGACY non-normalized basis reproduces its signed hash byte-exactly (433c: a2d2868c7669f5a2, 9d07: c1fcc7167f8b4174, a584: 098868b83165e82c, d3ed: a012e6aa44420bec), while post-330c child 1e95 (28dcf88ff9428cf6) matches only the normalized recompute — ruling out actual post-close edits (no EDIT events after each child's SIGNATURE) and the material_fingerprint=None-in-sidecar hypothesis (the close path always passes material=None to the sidecar; contrast ticket 51c1's sidecar also shows None). Legitimacy: defect — violates 330c's own AC #4 ('existing attestations ... remain valid') and the epic-level verdict-trust invariant (completion.py: a child's certified signature IS the trusted attestation). Fix: validity-on-read legacy-fingerprint fallback in compute_validity + observability (sidecar certifiable, stderr warning on withheld certification)."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785856799955904001,"uuid":"f0456e75-1b12-415d-8416-f1ebe2d42970"}